These fists do thunder, yet I'll not be dimmed—
The fire that burns shall blaze till dawn, not hold me down;
And when you draw breath at last, know I'll shake your hand.

plays.verse:
In defense of my blade and pride I stand and declare,
that this challenge ends where memory turns to blight;
let your words be shattered as I turn back the echo of your name—word by word, I say: "Witness!"? Not yet.

